{"parentUuid":"3c4824bd-bf0d-4da2-8f98-9fd426dafd60","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a37ab2812811a4b37","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfftfaSftX7Pybt6mpvky","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Model **v8zn** is built and in the worktree, but the job is not complete. Task 3, putting the air hoses into channels, was not done. The B drawer channel corner pieces were not done either. Everything else, including both of the coordinator's pano corrections, is done. Nothing committed, pushed or sent to coord.\n\n**WHAT WAS DONE**\n- **QR wiring:** three covered vertical channels now run behind the compartments (left, centre, right). They pass through holes in the compartment top plate and join the existing top distribution box. Every lock and sensor cable is now a short straight stub into the nearest channel, and the open horizontal cables behind the flaps are gone. The box feed cables over the top of the QR box and the 5 new customer-panel cables (screen, keypad/printer, reader) also run in covered channels. Power is red, data is blue.\n- **K right wall (#33/#81/#82):** these no longer pass through the pusher's path (y 1006–1109). They run along the wall in a channel above that band, down a rear vertical channel, under the belt, and reach the front sensor from above. The new channels and cables were checked against the pusher and cutter at every animation frame: no contact.\n- **K #83 (cutter bottom sensor):** the sensor is fixed, not on the moving cutter, so no energy chain is needed. The cable now runs in a slim vertical channel.\n- **B:** the four fan cables (#108, #109, #126, #127), the cooling unit supply (#40) and the B electrical box output now run in covered channels.\n- **Main panel back exit (coordinator's correction):**\n  - Cables leave through the existing back glands straight into a vertical channel directly behind the panel, with power and data in separate compartments.\n  - The channel runs along the U floor to the existing F back channel.\n  - Building and floor cables run in a top horizontal channel.\n  - Nothing goes into the oil tin's space; the only drop into F is the existing channel.\n  - The 3 side glands were removed and the holes closed.\n- **Main switch:** the switch body is now an ABB OT40F4 (4-pole 40 A, 48×56×68 mm) on the DIN rail in the empty slot from the old breaker. The door carries only an OHYS2AJ handle (65×65×48 mm, Ø22.5 door hole), connected by a 6 mm square OXP6X shaft. The building cable runs behind the mounting plate, through a rubber grommet, to the switch's top terminals on a fixed path. The old door hole has a blanking plug.\n- **Idle green hose end:** this was a leftover duplicate branch. I removed it and bridged the line to the compressor outlet.\n\n**CHECKS**\n- **Collisions:** new real collisions 0 (KANAL, KABLO and SAC groups, against v8zm).\n- **Cable crossings:** 0 for the QR, K and B checks and among the pano cables.\n- **Moving parts:** the K pusher and cutter (14 nodes) and the QR flap have no contact. The B drawer sweep check was still running when I stopped.\n- **Envelope and A:** nothing sticks out of any station, and nothing new is inside A.\n- **Labels:** 0 errors, 0 unlabelled.\n- **Floating parts:** only the customer-panel cables are flagged. The tool hides parts labelled as cover (kpk), and the panel parts carry that label, so the cables look unattached even though they touch the panel.\n- **Browser:** the page loads `?v=8zn`, the model is loaded with 6 animations, and there are no console errors.\n\n**STILL OPEN**\n- **Air hoses (task 3)** are still outside channels.\n- **B drawer channel corner pieces** (the 40–50 mm open joints) were not made. The rail's rear plate and flange take up that space, so the rail side needs changing first.\n- **Customer panel:** I assumed which cable goes to which panel part.\n- **Switch dimensions:** taken from distributor pages, not checked against an ABB datasheet. The ABB datasheet failed to download, and the shaft length was not checked against a catalogue.\n- **JSON cache-busting:** I changed only the GLB `?v` in the page, as instructed. The page's `mekanizma_v3_8.json` `?v` is unchanged, so a browser may serve the old JSON from cache.\n- Nothing has been moved into the generators.\n\n**FILES**\n- Worktree (`…\\worktrees\\claude-hat3-v8\\otonom\\`): `hat3d\\v3\\hat3_v8.glb`, `hat3d\\v3\\mekanizma_v3_8.json`, `hat3d\\v3\\parca_kutulari.json`, and `hat\\makine_v3_8.html` (only `8zm`→`8zn`).\n- Scratchpad: `S\\hat3_v8zn.glb`, scripts in `S\\elk5\\` (`b5run.py`, `qr5.py`, `k5.py`, `b5.py`, `p5.py`, `ekstra5.py`, `j_e6.py`), audit in `S\\elk5\\den7\\`. A summary is appended to `S\\gece\\DEGISIKLIKLER.md`.\n- Images (`S\\elk5\\`):\n  - `qr_ic_once.jpg`, `qr_ic_sonra.jpg`\n  - `k_sag_duvar.jpg`\n  - `b_fan.jpg`\n  - `hava_genel.jpg` (current state; hoses not yet in channels)\n  - `pano_ici_salter.jpg`\n  - `pano_arka_cikis.jpg`\n\nSources:\n- [ABB OT40F4N2 (RS)](https://int.rsdelivers.com/product/abb/ot40f4n2-1sca104932r1001/abb-4-pole-din-rail-isolator-switch-ip20-40a-560/6867275)\n- [ABB OT40F4N2 (ilecsys)](https://www.ilecsys.co.uk/products/abb/ot/ot40f4n2)\n- [ABB OHYS2AJ (Edwardes)](https://www.edwardes.co.uk/products/abb-ohys2aj-ip65-red-yellow-defeatable-handle-ot16-ot125f-switches)\n- [ABB OHYS2AJ (Expert Electrical)](https://www.expertelectrical.co.uk/abb-ohys2aj)\n- [ABB OXP6X290 shaft](https://www.amazon.com/ABB-OXP6X290-Pistol-Handle-Shaft/dp/B00JV3JRSS)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":504623,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2451,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":254},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":504623},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output